the name of colour for a colour is a text if
    red is equal to the colour
    and the text is equal to "Red"
    otherwise green is equal to the colour
    and the text is equal to "Green"
    otherwise blue is equal to the colour
    and the text is equal to "Blue".

the sum of list for a list is a number N if
    [] is equal to the list
    and N is equal to 0
    otherwise prolog (the list=[T|L])
    and the sum of list for L is a number M
    and N = T + M.

the first element else zero for a list is a number if
    [] is equal to the list
    and the number is equal to 0
    otherwise prolog (the list=[T|N])
    and the number is equal to T.

